# What stays out of the repository, and why.
#
# The rule applied here: ignore what can be regenerated, what is machine-
# specific, and what is a secret. Everything else is committed — including
# the image assets, because for a project whose only copy lives on one
# machine, git is the backup, and an ignored file is an unbacked-up file.

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
dist/
build/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The brain (and its DPAPI-encrypted provider keys) lives in ~/.dariusai,
# outside this tree — but a stray .env here would not be encrypted at all.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local state and databases ----------------------------------------------
# brain.db is the skill index; skills/ is its markdown store. Both belong to
# a brain directory, normally ~/.dariusai, but are ignored here in case one
# is ever created inside the repo. *.db also covers the data/app.db that
# workbench projects create.
#
# /skills/ is ROOT-ANCHORED deliberately. Written bare as `skills/` it matched
# every directory of that name at any depth — which silently excluded all 65
# files under addon/skills/, the library this project ships. The leading slash
# keeps the original intent (a brain store accidentally created at the repo
# root) without swallowing the addon tree.
brain.db
/skills/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3

# --- Runtime and tooling output ---------------------------------------------
# launch_error.log is written only when the launcher dies under pythonw.
# .dariusai-scratch/ is where run_snippet writes code blocks before running
# them. _dom_dump.html comes from the headless UI driver.
launch_error.log
*.log
.dariusai-scratch/
_dom_dump.html

# --- Build artifacts / bloat ------------------------------------------------
# 70+ MB packaged zips regenerated from the tree. Not committed — they
# double the clone size for every user and every clone forever, and they
# are trivially rebuilt from the source that is committed.
DariusAI.zip
Brain.zip
/*.zip

# --- Root-level screenshots -------------------------------------------------
# Dev screenshots (bug logs, layout drafts) at the repo root are local
# reference only — they add MB of noise for every user with nothing to
# show for it. Root-anchored so PNGs inside src/, addon/skills/ and
# similar are unaffected.
#
# The three PNGs on the ! lines below are re-included deliberately:
#   logo2.png  - splash-screen artwork. launch.pyw loads it unconditionally
#                (see line 29). Removing it made the desktop shortcut die
#                silently on every fresh install — pythonw has no console,
#                so the tkinter TclError just vanished. Do not gitignore
#                again without also making the launcher defensive.
#   brain.png  - the source image tools/make_icons.py reads to regenerate
#                brain.ico (window + taskbar) and favicon.png (web tab).
#                Anyone rebuilding icons needs it.
#   logo1.png  - marketing / documentation asset referenced by external
#                README material.
/*.png
!/logo2.png
!/brain.png
!/logo1.png

# --- Generated projects -----------------------------------------------------
# The workbench lives at C:/DariusAIWorkbench, outside this tree. This is a
# guard in case someone points workbench_root inside the repo.
DariusAIWorkbench/

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# --- Agent run artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded and generated during an early agent run, when the project root
# was still the working directory. Not part of the app. Rooted with a
# leading slash so a legitimately-committed file of the same name inside a
# subdirectory is unaffected.
/feed.json
/quakes.html

# --- Internal documentation --------------------------------------------------
# Only the README is published. The engineering record and the operating
# contract stay on this machine: they carry the defect list, the architecture
# notes and the working instructions, and none of that belongs in a shared
# checkout. Consequence, accepted deliberately: these files are NOT backed up
# by git, so they live and die with the local disk.
/CLAUDE.md
/dariusai-harnessUpdated.md
/dariusai-harnessOLD.md
/BrainFIX.md
/AuditFullMAX.md
/AGENT_CAPABILITY_FIX.md
/COMMAND_TEST.md
/AGENT_WORKSPACE_CONVENTION.md
/AGENTS.md
!/README.md

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   brain.png, logo2.png   - build inputs (icons, splash)
#   logo1.png, *.png notes - reference material worth keeping backed up
#   version_lock.json      - pairs the source fingerprint with its version
#   tools/, tests/         - the verifier and the suite are part of the app
